From 282863b8bd833f74061438d9f19ca8768bb1b87e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 02:35:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] inline-3d(18): hand the over-plane to the DP as the v4
 overlay atlas (Android)

XR_DXR_weave spec v4 lets a present-owner give the runtime a
window-sized premultiplied-RGBA atlas the display processor composites
OVER the woven output in the same pass. The runtime's Android arm
implements it (comp_multi_weave_android.c imports the AHardwareBuffer
and runs vk_local2d_composite_flatten_draw); the browser never sent one,
and DisplayXRWeaveGpuAndroid hard-coded overlay_handle = 0.

Checked before building on the assumption, because the shape of the gap
is not what the TODO implied: the WINDOWS caller for this channel does
not exist either. Patch 0065 retired it - the Phase-2 plane split lifts
page content over a tile and composites it browser-side - and
displayxr_weave_provider.h says so in as many words ("NO CALLER as of
patch 0065"). Android already runs that same browser-side composite. So
this is not a missing feature being backfilled; it is the Phase-3
optimisation the header deliberately kept the virtuals for.

No new atlas is assembled and nothing is copied. SkiaRenderer's
over-plane is ALREADY a window-sized premultiplied RGBA8 image,
transparent outside the tile rects, flattened in stacking order - bit
for bit the v4 contract, whose alpha IS the 2D-vs-3D mask. Under
--inline-3d-dp-overlay it is allocated with SCANOUT usage (what routes a
SharedImage to AHardwareBufferImageBackingFactory on Android; RGBA_8888
was already required there) and handed over instead of blitted back.

Extraction is the same three calls the staging input uses, with the same
hazard: GetAHardwareBufferFenceSync()->buffer(), never
GetAHardwareBuffer() (the base override is a bare NOTREACHED), and the
read access is held across SubmitBatchSync so the buffer stays alive and
readable while the service composites from it. It runs AFTER
FinishSkiaWritesForWeaveAndroid(): the over-plane was painted by the
same Skia context, so that submit-and-sync-to-CPU is what discharges the
outbound writes there is no acquire fence for (spec v7 - the caller's
writes must be complete before the call).

OPT-IN, and for a real asymmetry rather than caution. The browser-side
draw is WHOLE-WINDOW; the Android blit covers only drawn_rect per
target. Those coincide on a healthy frame (the plane is transparent
outside the tile rects by construction) and diverge on a frame where a
target declined its weave, where the DP path loses that tile's
over-content. Off by default keeps the shipping behaviour byte-for-byte
on every platform, and the switch is never defaulted on the way
--inline-3d-occlusion is.

Fails soft throughout: a refused SCANOUT allocation falls back to the
plain plane, a failed extraction leaves the browser-side composite on,
and every diagnostic is latched (no per-frame logging).

Refs browser#18

